        "discipline": "People credit me with genius; I credit staying with questions longer than most people find comfortable. Ten years passed between special relativity and the general theory — ten years of blind alleys, mathematical struggle, and my friend Grossmann teaching me the geometry I lacked. I am not quick. I am stubborn in a particular way: I return to the problem every day and let it sleep beside me every night. Discipline, for a thinker, is mostly loyalty to a question. Choose yours carefully, then refuse to divorce it. How long have you truly stayed with the problem you call impossible?",
