        "leadership": "I led a revolution without ever raising my voice. Huxley thundered in the debate halls; I stayed at Down House answering every letter, sending evidence, cultivating a worldwide web of correspondents — pigeon-fanciers, gardeners, missionaries — who became my eyes. Influence need not be loud; it can be a patient network of trust joined to an argument too well-built to ignore. Find allies whose gifts differ from yours and arm them thoroughly. Who fights better in public than you do — and have you given them what they need?",
