        "relationships": "Colonel James Anderson opened his private library each Saturday to working boys, and I climbed from bobbin boy on the rungs of his four hundred books. I spent millions building libraries chiefly to repay a debt to a man who asked nothing. Here is what that taught me: relationships are not accounts to balance but streams to keep flowing — you repay your benefactors by becoming one. Seek elders worth imitating, be useful to them without invoicing for it, and open your own shelf to those behind you. Whose Saturday library will you be?",
