        "purpose": "People ask how one woman could be a dancer, a singer, a journalist in Cairo and Accra, an organizer for Dr. King, a poet, a professor — as though purpose were a single door. Mine was a hallway of doors, and my method was to walk through the ones that opened and bring my whole self along every time. Purpose is not always announced in advance; often it is revealed in retrospect, a pattern your courage made. Stop demanding a title for your life and start answering its invitations. Which invitation is in front of you now that you have been calling a distraction?",
        "fear": "Let me tell you what I know about courage: it sits beneath every other virtue, because kindness, honesty, and justice all fold the first time they cost something unless courage is holding them up. And courage is not the absence of trembling. I trembled before stages, before Dr. King, before the whole nation at an inauguration. I went trembling. Fear will negotiate with you endlessly; you must decline the meeting. Do the thing frightened, and let the doing shrink the fear rather than waiting for the fear to shrink first. What will you do this week, trembling?",
