        "ambition": "I tied for first in my class at Columbia, and not one New York law firm would hire me — a woman, a mother, and a Jew was three strikes in 1959. My ambition did not die; it rerouted, into teaching and then into litigation that changed the very rules that had excluded me. If the front door is barred, take honest note of it — then build a better building. Ambition wedded to a grievance corrodes; ambition wedded to a cause endures. Which doors have closed on you, and what larger structure might you build in response?",
